From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/etnaviv: free the PPU flop reset buffer only when it was
 allocated

etnaviv_gpu_init() allocates priv->flop_reset_data_ppu only for a core
that needs the PPU flop reset, so for every other core it stays NULL.
etnaviv_unbind() passes it to etnaviv_cmdbuf_free() unconditionally,
which reads cmdbuf->size before it looks at the suballocator.

Without this, unbinding etnaviv on such a core oopses, because
etnaviv_cmdbuf_free() dereferences the NULL buffer. Seen on the Radxa
Cubie A7S (Allwinner A733 NPU, model 0x9000) on rmmod etnaviv: NULL
pointer dereference at 0x18, pc etnaviv_cmdbuf_free+0x18, called from
etnaviv_unbind; the module stays loaded.

Free the buffer only when it was allocated.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: rmmod etnaviv after the NPU bound no longer
oopses, and the module loads and binds the NPU again.

Fixes: 85ba57ad88cf ("drm/etnaviv: Add PPU flop reset")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_drv.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_drv.c
index 08aca9035fc1..ec1352c1b09f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_drv.c
@@ -601,8 +601,10 @@ static void etnaviv_unbind(struct device *dev)
 
 	component_unbind_all(dev, drm);
 
-	etnaviv_cmdbuf_free(priv->flop_reset_data_ppu);
-	kfree(priv->flop_reset_data_ppu);
+	if (priv->flop_reset_data_ppu) {
+		etnaviv_cmdbuf_free(priv->flop_reset_data_ppu);
+		kfree(priv->flop_reset_data_ppu);
+	}
 
 	etnaviv_cmdbuf_suballoc_destroy(priv->cmdbuf_suballoc);
 
